# Behavior and Combat System

Animals and creatures in Nibiru live by their own complex rules. Their artificial intelligence takes into account many environmental factors.

---

## Advanced Behavior and Needs

Creatures do not stand still — they have their own needs:
- **Sleep-wake cycle**: Most animals sleep at night, while nocturnal predators go out to hunt. [color=yellow]Sleeping animals have much worse hearing and vision[/color], making them easy targets.
- **Pack instinct**: Wolves and other pack predators never travel alone. If you attack one of them, its cry will attract the whole pack. Packs often have a leader that coordinates attacks.
- **Mood**: Animals have moods. A hungry or beaten animal will be angry and slower to tame. A well-fed and happy animal [color=green]learns much faster[/color] and defends its owner more actively.

---

## Perception and Combat

Each animal has individual vision and hearing parameters.
> [!TIP]
> **Stealth:** You can go unnoticed if you slowly approach an animal from behind — outside its field of view it won't notice you if you stay quiet!

